  {"id": "F1", "category": "quantifier", "severity": "medium", "decl": "exists_infinite_pairwise_nonisomorphic_propertyT_icc_groups_with_isomorphic_factors", "line": 214, "paper_ref": "Theorem 1.2", "explanation": "`(∃ n, IsICC (Γ n))` requires only one Γ_n to be ICC, whereas the paper asserts that every Γ_n is ICC. Mathematically, ICC of Γ_n follows from L(Γ_n) ≅ L(Λ) being a factor. However, the formal statement as written is weaker than the paper and does not directly assert the infinite ICC fiber.", "polarity": "lean weaker", "probe_idea": "Replace line 214 with `(∀ n, IsICC (Γ n))` and check that the proof still goes through."},
  {"id": "F2", "category": "coverage", "severity": "low", "decl": "exists_infinite_pairwise_nonisomorphic_propertyT_icc_groups_with_isomorphic_factors", "line": 208, "paper_ref": "Theorem 1.2 (moreover)", "explanation": "The claim that Γ_n has a subgroup isomorphic to Γ_0 of index 2^{4n} (commensurability) is not formalized.", "polarity": "lean weaker", "probe_idea": "Add `∀ n, ∃ K : Subgroup (Γ n), Nonempty (K ≃* Γ 0) ∧ K.index = 2^(4*n)`."},
  {"id": "F3", "category": "definition-mismatch", "severity": "low", "decl": "TracialGroupFactorsIsomorphic", "line": 179, "paper_ref": "Theorem 1.2", "explanation": "The isomorphism of group factors is encoded as an algebraic *-isomorphism with an ad hoc projection-supremum normality condition and trace preservation. Both extra conditions are automatic for II_1 factors, so this only strengthens the existential claim relative to plain L(G) ≅ L(H).", "polarity": "lean stronger", "probe_idea": null},
